EM Text Editor - Help File
==========================

This is the help file for the EM text editor. Press C-x C-c to exit this help.

BASIC NAVIGATION
================

Character Movement:
  Arrow Keys        - Move cursor in all directions
  C-b (Ctrl+b)      - Move left (backward)
  C-f (Ctrl+f)      - Move right (forward)
  C-p (Ctrl+p)      - Move up (previous line)
  C-n (Ctrl+n)      - Move down (next line)

Line Movement:
  C-a / Home        - Move to beginning of line
  C-e / End         - Move to end of line

Word Movement:
  M-f (Alt+f)       - Move forward by word
  M-b (Alt+b)       - Move backward by word

Buffer Movement:
  M-<               - Move to beginning of buffer
  M->               - Move to end of buffer

Page Scrolling:
  C-v / PageDown    - Scroll down by one page
  M-v / PageUp      - Scroll up by one page
  C-l               - Recenter view around cursor

SELECTION (MARK AND REGION)
===========================

  C-Space           - Set mark at cursor (start selecting)
  C-x C-x           - Exchange point and mark
  Shift+Left/Right  - Extend selection by character
  C-g / ESC         - Deactivate mark (cancel selection)

The region between mark and cursor is highlighted on screen.

While a selection is active, typing replaces it, and Backspace,
Delete, Enter or C-y (yank) remove it first.

KILLING AND YANKING (CUT / COPY / PASTE)
========================================

  C-w               - Kill (cut) region
  M-w               - Copy region
  C-k               - Kill from cursor to end of line
                      (repeat to also kill the newline and keep appending)
  C-y               - Yank (paste) last killed text

UNDO
====

  C-_ or C-/        - Undo last change (repeat to undo more)

SEARCH
======

  C-s               - Incremental search forward
                      Type to search, C-s again for next match,
                      Enter to stop at match, C-g to cancel and return.
                      Search wraps around the end of the buffer.

EDITING
=======

  Backspace         - Delete character before cursor
  C-d / Delete      - Delete character under cursor
  Enter/Return      - Insert newline and split line
  Any printable char - Insert character at cursor

FILE OPERATIONS
===============

Opening Files:
  C-x C-f           - Open file (find file), with Tab completion
                      Opening a directory shows it in Dired

DIRED (DIRECTORY LISTING)
=========================

  C-x C-d / C-x d   - Prompt for a directory and open it in Dired
                      (prefilled with the current file's directory;
                      an empty input opens the current directory)

Opening a directory (C-x C-f, C-x C-d or 'em somedir') lists its
contents in 'ls -al' format: permissions, links, owner, group,
size, modification time and name (symlinks show their target).
  Enter / f / e     - Open the file or directory on the current line
  ^                 - Go to the parent directory
  g                 - Refresh the listing
  n / p             - Move down / up
  C-s               - Search for an entry name
The listing is read-only; C-x C-f and C-x C-c work as usual.

Saving Files:
  C-x C-s           - Save current file (prompts for a name if new,
                      with Tab completion)

Exiting:
  C-x C-c           - Exit editor (with save prompt if modified)

COMMAND SYSTEM
==============

Command Mode:
  M-x               - Enter command mode
  M-x help          - Show this help file (read-only)

Read-Only Buffers:
  - Help file opens as read-only to prevent accidental modification
  - Status bar shows "RO" indicator
  - Editing operations show "Buffer is read-only" message
  - Navigation and reading work normally

MINIBUFFER
==========

All prompts (open, save, M-x, ...) share one line editor:
  Left/Right, C-b/C-f  - Move within the input
  C-a / C-e            - Beginning / end of input
  Backspace, C-d       - Delete before / under cursor
  C-k                  - Delete to end of input
  C-u                  - Clear the whole input
  C-g / ESC            - Cancel the prompt

File name completion (C-x C-f and Save as):
  Tab               - Complete the common prefix, then cycle candidates
  Shift+Tab         - Cycle backward
  Enter             - Accept the highlighted candidate
                      (a directory is entered and its contents listed)
The candidate list is shown next to the input; "~/" is expanded.

STATUS BAR
==========

The status bar shows:
- Current filename (or [NoName] for new files)
- "*" if the buffer is modified, "RO" if read-only
- "[mark]" while a selection is active
- Current line and column

TROUBLESHOOTING
===============

If meta keys (M-f, M-b, M-v, M-x) don't work:
- Try pressing Esc followed by the key
- On macOS Terminal/iTerm2, enable "Use Option as Meta key"

If you get stuck:
- Press C-g to cancel current operation
- Press C-x C-c to exit (with save prompt)
- Use M-x help to see this help again
